Corrected version:

```cpp
bool BHV_Survey::setParam(string param, string val)
{
  if(IvPBehavior::setParam(param, val))
    return true;

  param = tolower(param);

  if(param == "survey_radius") {
    if(!isNumber(val))
      return false;

    double radius = atof(val.c_str());
    if(radius <= 0)
      return false;

    m_radius = radius;
    return true;
  }

  return false;
}
```

MOOS-IvP-specific reason: behavior config lines are routed through `setParam()`, including standard `IvPBehavior` parameters such as `name`, `pwt`, `condition`, `updates`, `duration`, `endflag`, `runflag`, etc. If a custom behavior overrides `setParam()` but never calls `IvPBehavior::setParam()`, those standard behavior parameters are rejected or ignored by the helm.

Also, `atof()` alone is unsafe here because invalid strings become `0.0`, so `survey_radius = banana` could silently set the radius to zero. MOOS-IvP behavior params should validate numeric strings explicitly, usually with `isNumber()` and any domain checks needed.
